    "done_when": "tests/test_ensure_holds_one_reservation.py passes under the root .venv python. Each case runs in a temporary RECKON_HOME against a recording scheduler; no real sbatch, salloc, srun or scancel runs. Four cases. (1) Four separate processes, not threads, call ensure_reservation at once with no published record, and the recording scheduler logs exactly one allocation-obtaining request. All four return the same job id, and the unkeyed host-global record in reckon/crew/placement.py names it. (2) A probe that cannot complete, because the scheduler query fails or times out, is treated as unknown rather than absent. ensure waits and retries, submits nothing while the probe stays unknown, and reports the unknown after its bound. (3) A recorded allocation the probe reports alive is never replaced: ensure returns already-held and makes no request. (4) A recorded allocation the probe reports gone is replaced exactly once. The hold is made through reckon/crew/fleet_node.py (its hold script, submit, and find_allocation by job comment), not through a second hold path; the manifest names the functions reused. The cross-process claim uses an operation atomic between processes on the workstation, and the manifest names it. The declared negative control is executed and logged. The comment near reckon/crew/placement.py:344 that says the project is carried in the path is corrected. tests/test_crew_placement_reservation.py, tests/test_placement_steps_under_reservation.py, tests/test_reservation_is_shared_across_projects.py and the new test show 0 added failures between a base arm and a head arm. Every log sits under the run directory, headed with revision, tree and command and ending EXIT=, and each basetemp under /tmp is deleted after its arm. Out of scope, listed as follow_ons: calling ensure from placement resolution in reckon/crew/dispatch.py, and adopting 1277272.",
